<hr data-start="317" data-end="320" class="">
<h2 data-start="322" data-end="371" class=""><strong data-start="325" data-end="371">Integrative Framing and Critical Synthesis</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="373" data-end="441" class=""><strong data-start="377" data-end="441">Triadic Capitalist Modes as Logics of Extraction and Control</strong></h3>
<p data-start="443" data-end="589" class="">These three capitalist formations can be seen as <strong data-start="492" data-end="544">interlocking modalities of extractive governance</strong>, each targeting different domains of life:</p>
<ul data-start="591" data-end="1012">
<li data-start="591" data-end="726" class="">
<p data-start="593" data-end="726" class=""><strong data-start="593" data-end="620">Surveillance capitalism</strong> governs the <strong data-start="633" data-end="666">realm of meaning and behavior</strong>, converting lived experience into prediction and control.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="727" data-end="867" class="">
<p data-start="729" data-end="867" class=""><strong data-start="729" data-end="754">Chokepoint capitalism</strong> governs the <strong data-start="767" data-end="799">realm of access and exchange</strong>, erecting infrastructural and legal bottlenecks to extract rents.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="868" data-end="1012" class="">
<p data-start="870" data-end="1012" class=""><strong data-start="870" data-end="889">Necrocapitalism</strong> governs the <strong data-start="902" data-end="929">realm of life and death</strong>, profiting from exposure to suffering, precarity, and institutional abandonment.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1014" data-end="1133" class="">Their convergence signals a <strong data-start="1042" data-end="1068">mutation of capitalism</strong> from production-based to <strong data-start="1094" data-end="1111">control-based</strong> accumulation regimes.</p>
<hr data-start="1135" data-end="1138" class="">
<h3 data-start="1140" data-end="1170" class=""><strong data-start="1144" data-end="1170">Three Axes of Analysis</strong></h3>
