ent-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="bbb21437-b4e4-4a08-993d-35f2dd2db2a7" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="relative max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)] bg-token-message-surface rounded-3xl px-5 py-2.5"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Explain how these three frameworks can counteract the three capitalisms</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-12" data-scroll-anchor="false"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="7ce1f502-9216-445e-8553-fe5f10b2f24b" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="329" class="">Here is a structured explanation of how <strong data-start="40" data-end="56">Psychocinema</strong>, <strong data-start="58" data-end="83">Geometric Bayesianism</strong>, and <strong data-start="89" data-end="102">SpherePop</strong> can serve as conceptual <em data-start="127" data-end="146">counterstrategies</em> to <strong data-start="150" data-end="169">Necrocapitalism</strong>, <strong data-start="171" data-end="198">Surveillance Capitalism</strong>, and <strong data-start="204" data-end="229">Chokepoint Capitalism</strong>, respectively. Each offers a distinct epistemic resistance‚Äîpsychological, cognitive, or structural.</p>
<hr data-start="331" data-end="334" class="">
<h2 data-start="336" data-end="378" class="">I. <strong data-start="342" data-end="378">Psychocinema vs. Necrocapitalism</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="380" data-end="401" class=""><em data-start="384" data-end="398">Psychocinema</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="402" data-end="553" class="">A psychoanalytic cinematic framework that explores subconscious drives, repression, and the symbolic order through film, narrative, and visual culture.</p>
<h3 data-start="555" data-end="587" class=""><em data-start="559" data-end="584">Mechanism of Resistance</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="588" data-end="920" class="">Psychocinema enables critical reflection on death, violence, and systemic abandonment‚Äînot as spectacle, but as structured absence. It surfaces <strong data-start="731" data-end="757">unconscious complicity</strong> in systems of necrocapitalist governance (e.g., incarceration, militarization, racialized disposability) and reveals how cultural products normalize death-worlds.</p>
<ul data-start="922" data-end="1333">
<li data-start="922" data-end="1038" class="">
<p data-start="924" data-end="1038" class=""><strong data-start="924" data-end="949">De-represses the Real</strong>: Forces confrontation with what necrocapitalism erases or commodifies‚Äîpain, loss, death.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1039" data-end="1166" class="">
<p data-start="1041" data-end="1166" class=""><strong data-start="1041" data-end="1068">Symbolic Re-inscription</strong>: Rewrites death and precarity into public consciousness as <strong data-start="1128" data-end="1149">unresolved trauma</strong>, not collateral.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1167" data-end="1333" class="">
<p data-start="1169" data-end="1333" class=""><strong data-start="1169" data-end="1194">Restores Subjectivity</strong>: Rejects the necrocapitalist reduction of individuals to <strong data-start="1252" data-end="1265">bare life</strong> by foregrounding their inner worlds, phantasms, and meaning-making.</p>
</li>
</ul>
