<h2 data-start="1340" data-end="1400" class="">II. <strong data-start="1347" data-end="1400">Geometric Bayesianism vs. Surveillance Capitalism</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="1402" data-end="1432" class=""><em data-start="1406" data-end="1429">Geometric Bayesianism</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="1433" data-end="1607" class="">A cognitive-epistemological framework where inference is modeled as <strong data-start="1501" data-end="1555">movement through high-dimensional conceptual space</strong>, guided by sparse heuristics and structured priors.</p>
<h3 data-start="1609" data-end="1641" class=""><em data-start="1613" data-end="1638">Mechanism of Resistance</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="1642" data-end="1851" class="">Surveillance capitalism thrives on <strong data-start="1677" data-end="1701">passive datafication</strong> and statistical prediction. Geometric Bayesianism counters this by emphasizing <strong data-start="1781" data-end="1801">active inference</strong>, <strong data-start="1803" data-end="1824">contextual priors</strong>, and <strong data-start="1830" data-end="1850">semantic opacity</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="1853" data-end="2364">
<li data-start="1853" data-end="1968" class="">
<p data-start="1855" data-end="1968" class=""><strong data-start="1855" data-end="1884">Inference Over Prediction</strong>: Shifts focus from externally imposed predictions to internal cognitive navigation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1969" data-end="2095" class="">
<p data-start="1971" data-end="2095" class=""><strong data-start="1971" data-end="2011">Privacy via High-Dimensional Opacity</strong>: Reduces extractability by encoding behavior in <strong data-start="2060" data-end="2094">sparse, non-obvious heuristics</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2096" data-end="2219" class="">
<p data-start="2098" data-end="2219" class=""><strong data-start="2098" data-end="2125">Agent-Centered Learning</strong>: Empowers individuals to update their beliefs <strong data-start="2172" data-end="2218">based on meaning, not manipulable patterns</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2220" data-end="2364" class="">
<p data-start="2222" data-end="2364" class=""><strong data-start="2222" data-end="2251">Uncommodifiable Semantics</strong>: The richer and more geometrically curved the mental space, the harder it is to flatten into behavioral surplus.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2366" data-end="2369" class="">
<h2 data-start="2371" data-end="2418" class="">III. <strong data-start="2379" data-end="2418">SpherePop vs. Chokepoint Capitalism</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="2420" data-end="2438" class=""><em data-start="2424" data-end="2435">SpherePop</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="2439" data-end="2609" class="">A visual programming and symbolic reasoning environment based on nested soap-bubble-like expressions, enabling intuitive and recursive manipulation of logic and language.</p>
<h3 data-start="2611" data-end="2643" class=""><em data-start="2615" data-end="2640">Mechanism of Resistance</em>:</h3>
<p data-start="2644" data-end="2860" class="">Chokepoint capitalism relies on structural lock-in, proprietary standards, and control over expression channels. SpherePop offers a <strong data-start="2776" data-end="2827">recursive, open-ended expressive infrastructure</strong> that subverts these constraints.</p>
<ul data-start="2862" data-end="3476">
<li data-start="2862" data-end="3003" class="">
<p data-start="2864" data-end="3003" class=""><strong data-start="2864" data-end="2903">Transparent Symbolic Infrastructure</strong>: Makes computation and logic visible and manipulable, removing dependency on black-boxed platforms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3004" data-end="3120" class="">
<p data-start="3006" data-end="3120" class=""><strong data-start="3006" data-end="3027">Recursive Freedom</strong>: Empowers users to navigate, modify, and recompose meaning structures from first principles.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3121" data-end="3314" class="">
<p data-start="3123" data-end="3314" class=""><strong data-start="3123" data-end="3155">Expression Without Platforms</strong>: By enabling computation as <strong data-start="3184" data-end="3212">self-contained recursion</strong>, SpherePop decouples creativity from commercial chokepoints (e.g., app stores, publishing platforms).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3315" data-end="3476" class="">
<p data-start="3317" data-end="3476" class=""><strong data-start="3317" data-end="3342">Anti-Monopoly Grammar</strong>: Its open semantic structure resists enclosure‚Äîevery expression is a node in a rewriteable tree, not a product trapped in a platform.</p>
</li>
</ul>
