Let the generative model of an agent be defined as:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{G}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\arg</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{q} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\underbrace</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{E}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>q[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> q(s) - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> p(s, o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>)]}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Variational Free Energy}} = D</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{KL}}(q(s) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span> p(s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> o)) - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> p(o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Where:
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: latent (internal) states
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: observations
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> q(s) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: approximate posterior
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> p(s, o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: joint generative model

For each subagent‚ÄîPsychocinema (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\psi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>), Geometric Bayesianism (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>), and SpherePop (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>)‚Äîwe define expected free energy over trajectories as:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(x)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{E}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\underbrace</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ln</span></span><span> q(s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>) - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ln</span></span><span> p(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>, s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>x)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Epistemic + Extrinsic Value}}] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{for } x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\psi</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Each system minimizes its own path-dependent variational bound while remaining embedded within a coupled ecological manifold.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{3. QCQP Formulation (SpherePop Kernel)}

We consider an expressive agent optimizing symbolic composition logic under recursive constraints:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{minimize} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{2} x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 x + q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{subject to} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{2} x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i x + q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>T x + r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> 0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> i=1,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>,m </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Ax = b
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Where:
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: latent symbolic encodings
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> n} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: structural constraints for logical coherence
- Constraints represent:  
    - Symbolic consistency (syntax trees)  
    - Cognitive load minimization (entropy bounds)  
    - Expressive economy (minimum surface complexity)

*Convex relaxations* enable approximations under bounded expressive depth.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{4. Markov Blanket Partitioning}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> B = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>I, O, H, E</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> represent:
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> I </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: Internal states (beliefs, latent narratives)
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: Observable states (data inputs)
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> H </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: Hidden states (model dynamics)
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>: External states (environmental affordances)

Each subagent optimizes within its own Markov blanket:

| Subsystem           | Internal State       | Sensory Interface        | Motor Output              |
|---------------------|----------------------|---------------------------|----------------------------|
| Psychocinema (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\psi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>) | Affective schema      | Visual + narrative stimuli | Emotional disruption/reframing |
| Geometric Bayesianism (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>) | Belief manifold       | Noisy sensory inputs       | Belief updates             |
| SpherePop (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>) | Recursive logic kernel | Semantic-symbolic inputs   | Code / syntax manipulations |

The joint system is emergent:  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\psi</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>( </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\psi</span></span><span>)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Subject to:  
- Coupled priors  
- Inter-agent communication  
- Shared resource constraints (computation, attention, time)

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{5. Negentropy as Functional Outcome}

Define negentropy as the distance from maximum entropy:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N}(x) = H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>} - H(x) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> |X| - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i} p(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> p(x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Each agent minimizes uncertainty not through control, but through **constructive divergence** from the capitalist attractor basin:
- Psychocinema increases affective resolution.
- Geometric Bayesianism increases epistemic resilience.
- SpherePop increases symbolic autonomy.

Together, they maximize negentropy across affective-cognitive-symbolic axes.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{6. Notes on Implementation and Relaxation}

- Use **SDP relaxations** for approximating non-convex SpherePop constraints.  
- Model inference with **particle filtering** in Geometric Bayesianism.  
- Implement Psychocinema with **variational narrative models** (e.g., VAE-encoded cinematic embeddings).

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{7. Closing Remark}

This negentropic framework treats resistance not as reactive protest but as **autopoietic optimization**‚Äîagents maintaining their identity and coherence against hostile predictive infrastructures.

