<h2 data-start="381" data-end="454" class=""><strong data-start="384" data-end="454">Quadratic Programming Relaxations (QPRs): Taxonomy and Integration</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="456" data-end="486" class=""><strong data-start="460" data-end="484">Definition (Unified)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="487" data-end="837" class="">A <strong data-start="489" data-end="531">Quadratic Programming Relaxation (QPR)</strong> transforms a discrete, combinatorially hard problem into a <strong data-start="591" data-end="623">continuous quadratic program</strong> by relaxing integral, rank, or structural constraints. These relaxations enable tractable approximation via convex methods and yield <strong data-start="757" data-end="783">negentropic estimators</strong> of original system structure, intention, or identity.</p>
<hr data-start="839" data-end="842" class="">
<h3 data-start="844" data-end="890" class=""><strong data-start="848" data-end="888">I. QPR in Combinatorial Optimization</strong></h3>
<p data-start="891" data-end="1010" class=""><strong data-start="891" data-end="902">Purpose</strong>: Approximate solutions to NP-hard combinatorial problems by embedding them in a continuous quadratic space.</p>
<p data-start="1012" data-end="1036" class=""><strong data-start="1012" data-end="1035">Relaxation Strategy</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1037" data-end="1171">
<li data-start="1037" data-end="1113" class="">
<p data-start="1039" data-end="1113" class="">Replace discrete set-membership variables with continuous [0,1] variables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1114" data-end="1171" class="">
<p data-start="1116" data-end="1171" class="">Introduce <strong data-start="1126" data-end="1145">slack variables</strong> for violated constraints.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1173" data-end="1197" class=""><strong data-start="1173" data-end="1196">Example Application</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1198" data-end="1356">
<li data-start="1198" data-end="1356" class="">
<p data-start="1200" data-end="1356" class="">In <strong data-start="1203" data-end="1216">SpherePop</strong>, QPR approximates combinatorial symbolic expressions via relaxed node expansions (i.e. not every bubble needs to be popped, just weighted).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1358" data-end="1379" class=""><strong data-start="1358" data-end="1378">Negentropic Role</strong>:</p>
