<h2 data-start="424" data-end="491" class=""><strong data-start="427" data-end="491">Extended Framework: Quadratic Programming Relaxations (QPRs)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="493" data-end="521" class=""><strong data-start="497" data-end="519">Unified Definition</strong></h3>
<p data-start="522" data-end="927" class="">A <strong data-start="524" data-end="560">Quadratic Programming Relaxation</strong> is a technique that transforms a difficult or discrete optimization problem‚Äîsuch as a mixed-integer, polynomial, or non-convex problem‚Äîinto a <strong data-start="703" data-end="731">convex quadratic program</strong> by relaxing integrality, rank, or structural constraints. QPRs serve as <strong data-start="804" data-end="837">approximate inference engines</strong> in systems where exact symbolic resolution is computationally or semantically infeasible.</p>
<hr data-start="929" data-end="932" class="">
<h3 data-start="934" data-end="974" class=""><strong data-start="938" data-end="974">Domains of Application (7 Types)</strong></h3>
<hr data-start="976" data-end="979" class="">
<h3 data-start="981" data-end="1031" class=""><strong data-start="985" data-end="1029">1. Mixed-Integer Polynomial Optimization</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1032" data-end="1319" class=""><strong data-start="1032" data-end="1044">Use Case</strong>: Symbolic systems with both discrete structures and continuous parameters.<br data-start="1119" data-end="1122">
<strong data-start="1122" data-end="1136">Relaxation</strong>: Replace integer constraints with continuous domains and reduce polynomial expressions to quadratic form using auxiliary variables or Lasserre-type relaxations.<br data-start="1297" data-end="1300">
<strong data-start="1300" data-end="1316">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1320" data-end="1579">
<li data-start="1320" data-end="1579" class="">
<p data-start="1322" data-end="1579" class="">Models <strong data-start="1329" data-end="1347">hybrid systems</strong> like SpherePop + GB integration: where symbolic grammar and cognitive weights must co-evolve.<br data-start="1441" data-end="1444">
<strong data-start="1444" data-end="1464">Negentropic Role</strong>: Preserves <strong data-start="1476" data-end="1516">joint semantic-coefficient stability</strong> while enabling exploration of combinatorial symbolic variants.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1581" data-end="1584" class="">
<h3 data-start="1586" data-end="1625" class=""><strong data-start="1590" data-end="1623">2. Combinatorial Optimization</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1626" data-end="1853" class=""><strong data-start="1626" data-end="1638">Use Case</strong>: Discrete structural decisions (e.g., pathfinding, layout, cluster membership).<br data-start="1718" data-end="1721">
<strong data-start="1721" data-end="1735">Relaxation</strong>: Replace set constraints with convex continuous equivalents; allow fractional decision weights.<br data-start="1831" data-end="1834">
<strong data-start="1834" data-end="1850">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1854" data-end="2028">
<li data-start="1854" data-end="2028" class="">
<p data-start="1856" data-end="2028" class="">SpherePop structure selection; ‚Äúbubble popping‚Äù strategies.<br data-start="1915" data-end="1918">
<strong data-start="1918" data-end="1938">Negentropic Role</strong>: Enables <strong data-start="1948" data-end="1970">symbolic ambiguity</strong>‚Äîdecisions do not collapse prematurely into binary logics.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2030" data-end="2033" class="">
<h3 data-start="2035" data-end="2067" class=""><strong data-start="2039" data-end="2065">3. Integer Programming</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2068" data-end="2286" class=""><strong data-start="2068" data-end="2080">Use Case</strong>: Optimization over logical variables (e.g., true/false, on/off decisions).<br data-start="2155" data-end="2158">
<strong data-start="2158" data-end="2172">Relaxation</strong>: Substitute binary variables with real-valued proxies in [0,1]; reintroduce soft penalties.<br data-start="2264" data-end="2267">
<strong data-start="2267" data-end="2283">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2287" data-end="2445">
<li data-start="2287" data-end="2445" class="">
<p data-start="2289" data-end="2445" class="">Geometric Bayesianism belief modeling across binary ontologies.<br data-start="2352" data-end="2355">
<strong data-start="2355" data-end="2375">Negentropic Role</strong>: Supports <strong data-start="2386" data-end="2444">gradient-based reasoning in discrete belief landscapes</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2447" data-end="2450" class="">
<h3 data-start="2452" data-end="2495" class=""><strong data-start="2456" data-end="2493">4. Semidefinite Programming (SDP)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2496" data-end="2686" class=""><strong data-start="2496" data-end="2508">Use Case</strong>: Non-convex matrix problems, especially where rank constraints emerge.<br data-start="2579" data-end="2582">
<strong data-start="2582" data-end="2596">Relaxation</strong>: Drop rank condition, keep PSD (positive semidefinite) requirement.<br data-start="2664" data-end="2667">
<strong data-start="2667" data-end="2683">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2687" data-end="2862">
<li data-start="2687" data-end="2862" class="">
<p data-start="2689" data-end="2862" class="">Psychocinema‚Äôs affective symbolic matrix (multi-layered interpretive fields).<br data-start="2766" data-end="2769">
<strong data-start="2769" data-end="2789">Negentropic Role</strong>: Facilitates <strong data-start="2803" data-end="2824">symbolic polysemy</strong> and unresolved trauma representation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2864" data-end="2867" class="">
<h3 data-start="2869" data-end="2905" class=""><strong data-start="2873" data-end="2903">5. Polynomial Optimization</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2906" data-end="3086" class=""><strong data-start="2906" data-end="2918">Use Case</strong>: Highly nonlinear symbolic/semantic equations.<br data-start="2965" data-end="2968">
<strong data-start="2968" data-end="2982">Relaxation</strong>: Approximate with quadratized versions; often involves sum-of-squares techniques.<br data-start="3064" data-end="3067">
<strong data-start="3067" data-end="3083">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3087" data-end="3221">
<li data-start="3087" data-end="3221" class="">
<p data-start="3089" data-end="3221" class="">SpherePop‚Äôs high-order bubble systems.<br data-start="3127" data-end="3130">
<strong data-start="3130" data-end="3150">Negentropic Role</strong>: Supports <strong data-start="3161" data-end="3185">recursive expression</strong> with manageable logical complexity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3223" data-end="3226" class="">
<h3 data-start="3228" data-end="3264" class=""><strong data-start="3232" data-end="3262">6. Non-convex Optimization</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3265" data-end="3435" class=""><strong data-start="3265" data-end="3277">Use Case</strong>: Continuous domains with multiple minima/maxima.<br data-start="3326" data-end="3329">
<strong data-start="3329" data-end="3343">Relaxation</strong>: Introduce convex envelopes or slack variables to smooth local traps.<br data-start="3413" data-end="3416">
<strong data-start="3416" data-end="3432">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3436" data-end="3587">
<li data-start="3436" data-end="3587" class="">
<p data-start="3438" data-end="3587" class="">Navigating multi-hypothesis regions in Geometric Bayesianism.<br data-start="3499" data-end="3502">
<strong data-start="3502" data-end="3522">Negentropic Role</strong>: Preserves <strong data-start="3534" data-end="3559">cognitive flexibility</strong> in probabilistic inference.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3589" data-end="3592" class="">
<h3 data-start="3594" data-end="3655" class=""><strong data-start="3598" data-end="3632">7. Active Perceptual Inference</strong> (Implicit Extension)</h3>
<p data-start="3656" data-end="3824" class=""><strong data-start="3656" data-end="3668">Use Case</strong>: Markov blanket adaptation and symbolic interface tuning.<br data-start="3726" data-end="3729">
<strong data-start="3729" data-end="3743">Relaxation</strong>: Soft coupling between active, sensory, and hidden states.<br data-start="3802" data-end="3805">
<strong data-start="3805" data-end="3821">In Framework</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3825" data-end="3970">
<li data-start="3825" data-end="3970" class="">
<p data-start="3827" data-end="3970" class="">Boundary dynamics between Psychocinema/GB/SpherePop.<br data-start="3879" data-end="3882">
<strong data-start="3882" data-end="3902">Negentropic Role</strong>: Enables <strong data-start="3912" data-end="3950">adaptive engagement with ambiguity</strong> in the environment.</p>
</li>
</ul>
